 [{:section/type :communication-multiplied,
   :section/id 22,
   :section/title "Would they like a coffee?",
   :section/body
   ["¿A ellos les gustaría un café?"
    "You will remember this structure to you all it is pleasing / you all like Les gusta to you all it would be pleasing / you all would like Les gustaría As you may have guessed these structures can also be used to talk about the third person."
    "to them all it is pleasing / they like Les gusta to them all it would be pleasing / they would like Les gustaría When it is not obvious who is the object of the sentence Spanish speakers use these identifiers a ellos, a ellas (all females) and a ustedes to identify who is the object A ellos les gusta to them it is pleasing / them they like to them it is pleasing / them they (all women) like A ellas les gusta to you (all) it is pleasing / you all you like A ustedes les gusta A ellos les gustaría to them it would be pleasing / them they would like A ellas les gustaría to them it would be pleasing / them they (women) would like A ustedes les gustaría to you (all) it would be pleasing / you all you would like Again the best way to understand is to practice. So go ahead and practice understanding in exercise 25B and then use these structures to create Spanish in Exercise 25D."]}],
 :lesson/number 25,
